From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meenmachine1 <78238681+meenmachine1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:18:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Decompiler: an option to print only C a compiler accepts

- Shows: C that has to be rewritten before a C compiler takes it, which a
  matching decompilation (and anyone recompiling decompiled code) does
  by hand: `grec._0_4_` for bytes of a variable no field names, `_DAT_x`
  for a read wider than its symbol, a label or the last `case` of a
  switch with no statement after it (`case 5:` then `}`), and
  conversions between pointers and integers without a cast (`uint x =
  p;`, where GCC 14 makes -Wint-conversion an error).
- Cause: the printer's artificial names (PrintC::pushPartialSymbol's
  `_off_size_`, pushMismatchSymbol's `_` prefix) are for reading, label
  emission doesn't look at what follows, and CastStrategyC::castStandard
  leaves out casts C only warns about.
- Patch: a new print option, `compilablec` (off by default). With it on:
  - the bytes print as an lvalue C accepts, `*(T *)((char *)&grec + 4)`
    (T the varnode's type, or undefinedN), and `*(T *)&x` for a read
    wider than x;
  - a label whose block prints nothing is followed by `;`, and so is the
    last case of a switch when its block prints nothing;
  - castStandard (CastStrategy::setExplicitPointerCasts) casts every
    conversion between a pointer and an integer type and between
    pointers whose typed targets differ in kind.
- Seen on: ARMv5TE (Nintendo DS, CodeWarrior) code in a matching
  decompilation, and on x86-64 and AArch64 programs.
- Ghidra 12.1.4.

